From 2be934024fde33450d4bcdf0b8df60e796505e0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:46:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: big shaders on Xenos: live ranges for
 internal instrs, 12-bit exec address, larger tables

dEQP uniform_api.random.3 (a straight-line vertex shader with ~70
fetches, 143 uniforms and 93 immediates) hit four limits in turn:
- internal instructions (predicate setup, kills) got no live range
  (block_idx_free 0) and held their registers to the end of the shader,
  ~30 of 64 here: give every instruction a range at creation and keep
  internal predicate-stack uses in it;
- IR2_MAX_SCHED 0x400 -> 0x800, as IR2_MAX_INSTR;
- the CF exec address is 12 bits on Xenos (Xenia ucode.h); the a2xx
  struct had 9 + 3 reserved and wrapped past 512 instructions, so the
  fetch patch offsets pointed into garbage;
- fd2 immediates[64] overflowed silently: 128, with a compile error past.
Also fetch_info 64 -> 256 (asserted), and fetches lose their scheduling
priority over ALU once 48 registers are in use.

